---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// Outside tools. Each opens normally, in the same tab, and is marked as an outside site.
const outside = [
  { href: 'https://gtamap.io', name: 'gtamap.io', note: 'A map. Spoilers are hidden by default.' },
  { href: 'https://fullsweepmap.com', name: 'FullSweep', note: 'A map and checklists. Spoilers are hidden by default.' },
  { href: 'https://support.rockstargames.com', name: 'Rockstar Support', note: 'For account, sign-in and code problems.' },
];
---

<Base title="About" description="How this guide handles spoilers and sources, and who it is not.">
  <h1>About this guide</h1>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Spoilers</h2>
    <p>
      The guide has one spoiler dial at the top of every screen. It starts on Off. Off shows answers that
      carry no spoilers. Places adds spots on the map. Mild adds small details.
    </p>
    <p>
      Hidden text is not in the pages you load at the default setting. It sits in separate files that the
      app fetches only when you ask. An answer with a hidden detail says so, for example "1 mild detail
      hidden", and you tap to show it. Showing one detail does not change the dial.
    </p>

    <h2>Where facts come from</h2>
    <p>
      Every answer links to its sources and shows the date we last checked them. We restate facts in our
      own words. Each answer also carries a confidence level:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Official.</strong> A Rockstar, Take-Two, PlayStation or Xbox page says it, and we read that page.</li>
      <li><strong>Reported.</strong> A news outlet or creator says it and cites a source, but no official page confirms it.</li>
      <li><strong>Community.</strong> Players report it. Treat it as likely, not certain.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If we could not find a source, there is no answer. We do not guess.</p>

    <h2>Maps and help</h2>
    <p>We link to better tools instead of rebuilding them.</p>
  </div>
  <ul class="tap-list outside">
    {outside.map((o) => (
      <li>
        <a href={o.href} rel="noopener noreferrer">
          <span class="name">{o.name}</span>
          <span class="note">{o.note}</span>
          <span class="tag">outside site</span>
        </a>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Unofficial</h2>
    <p>
      This is an unofficial fan project. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by Rockstar Games or
      Take-Two Interactive. It uses no Rockstar logos, art or fonts.
    </p>

    <h2>Your progress and privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing here is tracked: no analytics, no ads, no accounts. The one cookie is the sign-in cookie that
      lets you past the password page.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you are signed in, your ticked to-dos are copied to this site's own private store, so they follow
      you from one device to another. Nothing else is sent. Your spoiler setting, console, theme and stage
      stay on this device, so every new device starts with spoilers off.
    </p>
    <p>
      On the Checklist screen you can also copy your ticks as a code and paste it into another device. The
      code holds ticks only.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { max-inline-size: 40rem; }
  .prose h2 { margin-block: var(--space-5) var(--space-2); }
  .prose p, .prose ul { margin-block: 0 var(--space-3); }
  .prose ul { padding-inline-start: var(--space-5); display: grid; gap: var(--space-2); }
  .outside { max-inline-size: 40rem; margin-block-end: var(--space-3); }
  .outside a { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; column-gap: var(--space-3); align-items: center; }
  .outside .name { font-weight: 600; }
  .outside .note { grid-column: 1; color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--text-small); }
  .outside .tag { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1; font: var(--text-small) / 1 var(--font-mono); color: var(--muted); }
</style>
